{#
  Results.

  NO INVENTED STATISTICS. Every metric on this page is a bracketed placeholder
  and is meant to look like one: [+XX%], [XX%], [X.X]. A plausible-looking
  figure would be a fabricated claim the moment it shipped, and CLAUDE.md puts
  claims content outside anything auto-generated. Each stat also carries a
  bracketed source line, because design.md requires stats to be sourced and
  dated, so an unsourced number cannot quietly pass review.

  The narrative bodies are bracketed placeholders too. The handoff carried
  lorem ipsum there; bracketed English is used instead so placeholder copy and
  placeholder numbers read as the same deliberate state rather than one looking
  like filler and the other like data.

  Ayres Hotels is named, with a real attributed quote. The other two clients
  are bracketed and anonymous until named permission exists.

  Work samples are framed as documents, not photographs: bordered, on a light
  panel, with browser chrome where appropriate. That keeps them visually
  separate from the black and white photomontage system.

  No alt-glyph: no headline here has a swap justified by what the word means.
#}
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}
{% from "components/section.njk" import section %}
{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}

{% call section(containerClass="cs-lead", orient="Chosen results") %}
  <div class="cs-lead__figure">
    <img src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-shears-landscape.webp"
         alt="Shears, strategic subtraction"
         width="440" height="320" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
    <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--lead" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h1 class="cs-lead__headline">{{ lead.headline }}</h1>
    <p class="cs-lead__lede">{{ lead.lede }}</p>
  </div>
{% endcall %}

{% for case in cases %}
  {#- ONE NAME FOR ALL THREE CASES, and the per-case quote deliberately carries
      none. Both of these blocks are inside the loop over cases, so an orient on
      the quote would render between cases and the header would read
      Selected work, In a client's words, Selected work as you scrolled one
      list. A case and the quote inside it are the same place. -#}
  {% call container(class="pb-16", orient="Selected work") %}
    <div class="cs-case">
      <div>
        <p class="cs-eyebrow">{{ case.meta }}</p>
        <h2 class="cs-case__title">{{ case.title }}</h2>
        <p class="cs-case__challenge">{{ case.challenge }}</p>
        <p class="cs-case__body">{{ case.body }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-stat p-0">
        <span class="cs-stat__value">{{ case.stat.value }}</span>
        <span class="cs-stat__label">{{ case.stat.label }}</span>
        <span class="cs-stat__source">{{ case.stat.source }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {% if case.sample %}
      <div class="mt-16">
        {% if case.sample.kind == "browser" %}
          <figure class="cs-sample m-0">
            <div class="cs-sample__chrome">
              <span class="cs-sample__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="cs-sample__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="cs-sample__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="cs-sample__url">{{ case.sample.url }}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-sample__slot">
              <p class="cs-sample__note">{{ case.sample.note }}</p>
            </div>
          </figure>
        {% else %}
          <div class="cs-samples--pair">
            {% for note in case.sample.notes %}
              <figure class="cs-sample cs-sample--card m-0">
                <div class="cs-sample__slot">
                  <p class="cs-sample__note">{{ note }}</p>
                </div>
              </figure>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  {% endcall %}

  {% if case.quote %}
    {% call container(narrow=true, class="pb-16") %}
      <blockquote class="cs-pullquote m-0">
        {{ case.quote.body }}
        <cite>{{ case.quote.cite }}</cite>
      </blockquote>
    {% endcall %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<div class="cs-fruit">
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--fruit cs-rule--fruit-l" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--fruit cs-rule--fruit-r" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% call container() %}
    <img class="cs-fruit__figure"
         src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-fruit-portrait.webp"
         alt="Ripe cluster, the payoff of tended growth"
         width="1120" height="640" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{% call container(class="cs-close pt-22") %}
  <p class="cs-close__note">{{ close }}</p>
  {{ button("Start a conversation", href="/contact/") }}
{% endcall %}
